{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/279005-is-halloween-a-special-day-in-your-chronicle","id":279005,"title":"Is Halloween a special day in your chronicle?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-12T13:36:06-07:00","id":279005,"title":"Is Halloween a special day in your chronicle?","content":"In the long-running <i>Changeling</i> game I'm in, we just did our Halloween story.* In it, the characters were surprised by an envoy from the Hedge, who want our artist character to stop painting gateways into places and times, lest they fall into the hands of the artist's former Keeper. In exchange, they offered our characters the information to rescue the minor hedge god who helped the artist escape.<br /> <br /> That wasn't the big thing, though. The big thing is that my character's Keeper has been a complete mystery, because my character only remembers her many attempts to escape, not what she was escaping <i>from</i>. Through the artist's paintings, we found out that my character actually has/will go in and out of the Keeper's pocket of Arcadia many times in her life, and that the Keeper experiences them in a different order from my character. Perhaps the worst revelation is that sometime in the future, my character will go with the Keeper on purpose.<br /> <br /> Do you do anything special for Halloween? What's happened in your games?<br /> <br /> <br /> (* We don't sync with the real time of year, it just happened by coincidence that October in our game matched up with real October.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T13:59:48-07:00","id":279049,"title":"","content":"Never did one since Halloween is not a cultural tradition of my country, at least for my generation. Surely those young ones get Americanized.<br /> <br /> Running special event makes more sense during those folk festival rooted here even before Christianity, like that one we have on June.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T16:27:53-07:00","id":279154,"title":"","content":"I generally run themed games for holidays around the time of the holiday. In my Dresden game, we had Black Peter (Knight of Christmas) ask the PCs to assist in thwarting the Krampus. Generally, sessions near to Halloween have more monsters and horror elements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T17:33:37-07:00","id":280283,"title":"","content":"I have always either attempted to fit a specific Halloween themed session in an ongoing campaign, or I will setup a one-off session for the day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;30 pieces of silver and a deal's a deal&quot;</i> - Nothing's Free, Alice Cooper","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4073-lrdvampyre","name":"lrdvampyre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4073_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T21:27:56-07:00","id":281915,"title":"","content":"In some of my settings, Halloween is the one night of the year that you *know,* without a doubt, that the Wild Hunt will be not only out, but out in its fullest force. Autumn often holds a big costume bash and rents out whole wings of hotels and suchlike, just to make sure nobody goes out in it. <br /> <br /> well, except for the bravest/strongest/stupidest Autumn courtiers, of course. They go up on the roof with binoculars and notepads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T01:59:51-07:00","id":282061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/279005-is-halloween-a-special-day-in-your-chronicle?p=281915#post281915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In some of my settings, Halloween is the one night of the year that you *know,* without a doubt, that the Wild Hunt will be not only out, but out in its fullest force. Autumn often holds a big costume bash and rents out whole wings of hotels and suchlike, just to make sure nobody goes out in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>But wouldn't his mean that Wild Hunt could steal people in costumes from the streets? As True Fae pointing on innocent child: &quot;oh, look, so adorable Darkling right there&quot;...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T19:10:30-07:00","id":283059,"title":"","content":"Well, the costumes were originally intended to &quot;scare away evil spirits,&quot; y'know.<br /> <br /> As for whether it works, well... who knows if any of that stuff works?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","user":"HobbitGuy1420","date":". 10-15-2014, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T15:30:05-07:00","id":284283,"title":"","content":"I think I may have halloween be the end date for the hunt of leaves in a chronical I'll be running, where the &quot;victims&quot;(loyalists,malevolent hobgoblins,etc.) of the hunt are brought before the Autumn King and he reminds the freehold why it should be afraid of him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Do the dead dare walk the Earth before my eyes? Will the undead raise an army, fall in, and advance? Will those who would abandon God and embrace the heretical order DARE to presume to meet my gaze!? Iscariot will not allow it. <b>I</b> will not allow it.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3889-ninjasantaclause","name":"Ninjasantaclause","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T16:28:50-07:00","id":284338,"title":"","content":"We have actually not had Halloween happen in a Changeling (or WoD) game yet, outside special sessions I've run on Halloween.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T02:32:36-07:00","id":284789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/279005-is-halloween-a-special-day-in-your-chronicle?p=283059#post283059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the costumes were originally intended to &quot;scare away evil spirits,&quot; y'know.<br /> <br /> As for whether it works, well... who knows if any of that stuff works?</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see this that True Fae see all the time past the Mask - so they can't discern if devils and ghouls before them are real changelings or mortal only dress as those. And as Wild Hunt want to capture humans, it makes it very unfortunate for Fae.<br /> <br /> It also lead to nice story seed and old legend - those children and adult the <b>don't</b> celebrate Halloween are easy pray for Lords. <i>You shouldn\u2019t go alone without costume on All Hallows Eve, or wicked will get you\u2026 </i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T16:02:51-07:00","id":285476,"title":"","content":"Wow it must have been two years ago now. <br /> <br /> Our motley was at odds with the main freehold in the area.<br /> <br /> The King of the freehold was a cold loyalist, who no one believed was a loyalist. He had it out for one of our motley on a personal level (their Keeper was playing a game), and invited us to what would clearly be a trap. However, his messenger said we could bring along people if we didn't feel safe going on our own.<br /> <br /> So we brought everyone. We organized a huge Halloween party, got a couple bands, got invites out all over the local college and high schools and social media, someone even arranged a deal with the goblin market to sort of stretch into the party grounds. We got caught up in sticking it to the leader of the freehold, so we didn't really get to enjoy much of the party ourselves. It was over a year ago, but the highlights were a powerful spring court exile getting up on stage to perform, all sorts of hedge-drugs, this mysterious tattoo artist from the goblin market having a stall and doing his business (he took flesh for payment and pigment), dodging a hunter cell who was just barely aware of the existence of other worlds but didn't realize we were changelings, some time travel when we dodged the folks the King sent to catch us at the party and managed to get to his freehold just as he was sending them, and finding out the King had an army of skeletons. We also had t-shirts made.<br /> <br /> Later we found out about three dozen people went missing, most taken by the King. And we had gained the attention of a nasty pack of True Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T12:29:49-07:00","id":288769,"title":"","content":"So I got idea to run Mortals one-shot game about Halloween using <b>Changling's</b> background for our game club this year - in the little town Somewhere in Maine few people don't like Halloween ( it's needed from PCs for story logic ). I want them to confront with Wild Hunt and been taken for not being dressed up - because in my WoD, costumes protected humans from being kidnapped.<br /> <br /> Question is this: <b>Are there any other interesting Halloween stories and tradtions that could be used with <i>Changling</i>-kind game?</b> Trick or Treat'ing I use as Changlings mean for protection from Gentry. Are there other traditions? I'm from Poland, I only know All Hallows Eve from movies and books. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm even tempt to use <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/285890-goblin-hedge-settlement-halloween-town\">Halloween Town</a> for the later part of game that character will be freeing themselves - or stumble upon the aid of rescuing the taken comrades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-21-2014, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T12:51:55-07:00","id":288807,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mischief_Night\" target=\"_blank\">Pranks and mischief</a>. Egging/toilet papering houses, random vandalism. Sometimes it can get pretty bad, you can look up <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Devil%27s_Night\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Night</a>.<br /> <br /> If you're too old for trick or treating, some people and theme parks set up seasonal scare attractions, like haunted houses with actors to chase you around with chainsaws. Many of these are oriented for teens and adults.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.cracked.com/article_19509_5-halloween-parties-too-badass-to-be-real-that-totally-are.html\" target=\"_blank\">Parties, too.</a> Though this link is more about attractions.<br /> <br /> And since it's the World of Darkness, and Changeling, I should point out there's a lot of urban legends about things like tampered candy given out. Poisoned candy, fruit (particularly apples) with needles or razor blades in them, that sort of thing. Things like that have happened but not to the breadth the urban legends would make out. Right now with marijuana legalized in Colorado some people are freaking out about it there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-21-2014, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T03:53:00-07:00","id":295701,"title":"","content":"For my general games ( and tomorrow session ) I made nice in-setting idea\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Arcadia's Laws of Halloween</b><br /> Probably made by first Autumn Royality with Faeire itself, those precepts are protecting both humans and changlings from being taken by Wild Hunt, that is especially often on All Hallows Eve. On this time of thee year, the veil between Earth and Arcadia is very thin and Gentry looking for they Wild Hunts, mainly for new humans slaves to be changed in to the Other. But if you are respecting those Laws, you will be safe - only most humans just don't remember why those Laws were laid, and treat them as harmless play. They also isn't just simple to broken - most of the time you need to word that you are all intentions on breaking them.<br /> <br /> <b>Arcadia's Laws of Halloween:</b><br /> <b><b>1. Don't be alone.</b><br /> <b>2. Disguise.</b><br /> <b>3. Don't break traditions.</b></b><br /> <br /> <b>First Law's</b> meaning is simple - strength in numbers. You are safer in larger crowd. Also, True Fae are sensing weakness, particularly in that night, and being alone is viewed as such. There are tale even that sometimes being only in small group of people is not enough and is treated as violation of the First Law. So better take the invites and go to those big parties and balls \u2013 Autumn Court is making one each Halloween for your safety. Or if you need to spend time with humans, just go to large event \u2013 more crowded, the better. The problem is if you reject the invitation.<br /> <br /> <b>Second Law\u2019s</b> meaning is more obscure \u2013 it\u2019s connected to the way True Fae perceive reality. Gentry always see the world past the Mask, so they see changlings Mein all the time. But when humans disguise in costumes as ghouls and goblins, the Others can\u2019 see the difference. As most Wild Hunts are made to get new slaves, so mortals are most seized trophy. If it is not the case, still is better to mix with crowd of disguised mortals that looks like Losts army, than to be the one alone, don\u2019t you think?<br /> <br /> <b>Third Law\u2019s</b> meaning is connected to the magic of the holiday. Beside the First and Second Law, this day has come to many smaller traditions that reproduce the behavior of Gentry \u2013 giving sweets to thee strangers, doing pranks and mischiefs, even calling down the dead. All this makes you look as one of Loyalist to the True Fae, one of their own. And so they will leave you be it.<br /> <br /> <b>Rules:</b> When character is clearly points out with the word ( or sometimes even very strong deed is enough) breaking of one Law, Others will become interested in him. Depending on the power and nature of the Gentry - and the protective magic contained in this Freehold - it can be from one to five offenses. Usually, however, there is principle of the three offenses - where a third evokes the Wild Hunt on character. Every breaking of Laws, offender gets a signal from the Others that did offense - even if she does not understand the message. Offences can be of the same kind or different types<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><i>Example: </i></b><i>Connor is jock, leader of local high school football team. He was planning to go on to this big party with his girlfriend and pals on Halloween, because he get invited, but they fight earlier that day and he said to her he don\u2019t go. On the return to home Connor see the weird shadow of giant dog or wolf, going like from nowhere. He just assumes he was overseeing something. </i><br /> <i>When return to his home, his mother asking him if will disguise himself. Even if Connor has costume ready, he says he would not dress up. He sits on the couch and watch scary movies. In one time on this creepy werewolf flick, he hear load howling. His mother in the kitchen says she didn\u2019t hear anything. Little scared, he plays on his console.</i><br /> <i>Later this night the Trick or Treaters come to his house. Being a bit angry on the holiday itself, he runes the kids from his porch. He then hear few howlings at once. He returns to home, to take the trash for his mother. When he is outside, back of the house, he see three hounds made of shadows that want to eat him alive! He throws a bag and run, in the woods, where the Arcadian Huntsman is waiting for him to be\u2026</i><br /> <br /> I hope it\u2019s cool addition to the games and nice little story generator. I can\u2019t wait for tomorrow\u2019s game session, as my players will play guys hating Halloween. I suspect so much fun with this idea\u2026 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T18:21:23-08:00","id":300623,"title":"","content":"We had Halloween HunterxChangeling crossover.<br /> <br /> &gt;my character dressed up as Catholic priest in mirrorshades and trenchcoat<br /> &gt;others dressed too in various get ups<br /> &gt;chased by Wild Hunt lead by a Kindly One which looks like Robert Baratheon on a motorbike<br /> &gt;some Beast Kith wolf eared Changeling NPC being chased too<br /> &gt;meanwhile I nearly make him go crazy, claiming I'm a federal agent infiltrating Catholic Church conspiracy called Brotherhood of Celestial Torch and asking him if he did not see any spider robot (which was actually an Angel)<br /> &gt;I and my team got chased into dead end<br /> &gt;The Keeper cornered us<br /> &gt;One of our PCs shot him in the eye with exceptional success<br /> &gt;Other PC scored exceptional success with cold iron knife and dusted King Robert<br /> &gt;The changeling all &quot;WTF&quot;<br /> &gt;Tries to escape<br /> &gt;We catch him and interrogate him (poor guy)<br /> &gt;Thankfully in spite of best intents of one of our PCs and my character's paranoia he is his sister's sec